Homepage: http://www.pnetlab.com/
Description: QEMU runtime for PNetLab (thin metapackage on stock Ubuntu QEMU)
 Thin metapackage that pulls in Ubuntu 26.04's own QEMU (qemu-system-x86,
 qemu-system-common, qemu-utils) — the same set the offline installer's apt
 step already installs — and wires the engine's expected /opt/qemu default
 path to it via an idempotent postinst (a compat tree of symlinks mirroring
 installer step [8/14]).
 .
 This package carries NO QEMU binaries of its own. It replaces (same package
 name, higher version) the opaque legacy rider pnetlab-qemu_6.0.0-30noble2,
 which shipped the frozen focal-built version zoo /opt/qemu-1.3.1 .. 7.2.0.
 On upgrade from that rider the maintainer scripts preserve the zoo on disk
 (as unowned files) so node templates pinned to a legacy qemu_version keep
 working; ownership/delivery of the zoo itself moves to the Phase-2
 core-assets channel. See docs/pnetlab-qemu-transition-design.md.
 .
 Architecture is amd64 (not all) to match the rider this package replaces and
 the amd64-only publication contract of debs/publish-codeberg.sh.
